  "agentNotes": [],
  "description": "Six tools screened against primary sources for one question: does it keep an immutable, user-attributed, append-only record of business decisions in its freely-licensed edition? Three have a real gap ",
  "orientation": "Six tools screened against primary sources for one question: does it keep an immutable, user-attributed, append-only record of business decisions in its freely-licensed edition? Three have a real gap (Alfresco, n8n, ERPNext/Frappe) and none of them paywalls audit - the capability simply is not what they built. Three do not: Flowable and Camunda shipped the feature, Odoo ships it free and forces it on in Germany. Read the two cross-cutting notes first; they carry the method. Where a slot is closed the discriminator moves from capability to procurability, which is a different question than the screen asks.",
  "openQuestions": [
    "Odoo already ships field-level attribution free and default-on, leaving only a hardening gap: do we drop the attribution pitch and keep Odoo as an integration target through the webhook seam, or drop Odoo from the deck?"
  ],
